 "standard_text": "Expand algebraic expressions with brackets; expand the product of two binomials; factorise expressions by taking out common factors. (summary of the NERDC JSS 2 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 2 maths worksheets on algebra: expanding single brackets, simplifying, expanding two brackets and factorising by common factors. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "a(b + c) = ab + ac",
 "key_sub": "Factorising undoes expanding.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Multiply every term inside the bracket by the term outside: 3(2x − 5) = 6x − 15.</li><li>(x + 3)(x + 5) = x² + 5x + 3x + 15 = x² + 8x + 15.</li><li>To factorise, take out the HCF of the terms: 6x + 9 = 3(2x + 3).</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Expand 4(3a − 2) − 2(a + 1)</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>12a − 8 − 2a − 2</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 10a − 10</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Factorise 8y² − 12y</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>HCF is 4y</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 4y(2y − 3)</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Multiplying only the first term</td><td>Multiply every term in the bracket.</td></tr><tr><td>Sign errors with a negative outside</td><td>−2(a + 1) = −2a − 2.</td></tr><tr><td>Not taking out the HCF</td><td>Take out the biggest common factor.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is a binomial?",
   "a": "An expression with two terms, like x + 4."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I check a factorisation?",
   "a": "Expand it again."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is x × x?",
   "a": "x²."
  }
